# Profile-bundle (RDMF v3 `profileFiles`) path corpus — ONE list for both
# validators: render-deploy-manifest.py `profile_file_path_error` /
# `validate_profile_files` (infra, the producer) and manifest.nim
# `profileFilePathError` / `validateProfileFiles` (reprobuild, the agent).
# tests/unit/test-deploy-manifest.sh case 16 feeds every line to the Python
# side; reprobuild's manifest tests are expected to read this same file (or a
# verbatim copy, checked equal) so the two implementations cannot drift.
#
# Format, one case per line, fields separated by a single TAB:
#   ok    <path>                 the path is accepted on its own
#   bad   <path>                 the path is refused on its own
#   setok <path> <path> ...      the set of paths is accepted together
#   setbad <path> <path> ...     the set is refused (each path valid alone)
# Escapes in a path: \t TAB, \0 NUL, \\ backslash; the field `<empty>` is the
# empty string (a bare empty field would be trailing whitespace). Blank and #
# lines are ignored.
ok	locks/node-exporter.lock
ok	fleet.hosts
ok	a/b/c.lock
ok	.hidden
ok	..dotdot-prefix.lock
ok	locks/x..y.lock
ok	with space.lock
ok	unicode-ünïcödé.lock
ok	manifest_profile.nim.bak
bad	<empty>
bad	/abs.lock
bad	//double-leading.lock
bad	a//b.lock
bad	a/./b.lock
bad	./a.lock
bad	a/../b.lock
bad	../escape.lock
bad	..
bad	.
bad	trailing/
bad	back\\slash.lock
bad	nul\0byte.lock
bad	manifest_profile.nim
bad	locks/manifest_profile.nim
setok	locks/a.lock	locks/b.lock	fleet.hosts
setbad	locks/a.lock	locks/a.lock
setbad	locks	locks/a.lock
setbad	locks/a.lock	locks
setbad	a/b	a/b/c
